'''Klatooinians''' were a [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Klatooine]], who often worked as henchmen and [[bounty hunter]]s. Klatooinians possessed a strong physique that led many of them to work in the criminal underworld. Some Klatooinians included [[Barada]] and [[Kithaba]], who both worked for [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]].

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:Klatooinian_drinking_Spotchka.png|thumb|left|250px|A Klatooinian raider drinking spotchka]]
Klatooinians were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[humanoid]] [[species]] from the [[planet]] [[Klatooine]]<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> in the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="TFABG">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]]</ref> Klatooinians were common throughout [[the galaxy]]. They were distinguishable through their prominent brows and visible [[Tooth|teeth]]. Klatooinians possessed a strong build, which made them useful laborers.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> Klatooinians' skin [[color]] ranged from green to brown,<ref name="Klatooinian" /> and they had green [[blood]].<ref name="Chapter 5">{{BOBF|Chapter 5: Return of the Mandalorian}}</ref> Their natural habitat was a [[desert]] or wasteland.<ref name="VE" /> Klatooinians could also be [[force-sensitive]].<ref name="Alien Archive" />

==Klatooinians in the galaxy==
Their strong build and menacing appearance drew many Klatooinians to work in the underworld as [[bounty hunter]]s, henchmen, and [[bodyguard]]s. Many Klatooinians were also sold into [[slavery]] due to their skills as laborers. [[Tarados Gon]] was a force-sensitive Klatooinian who joined the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Alien Archive" />

[[Castas]] was a [[Gender|male]] Klatooinian bounty-hunter who was active during the [[Clone Wars]]<ref name="Castas">{{Databank|castas|Castas}}</ref> and worked alongside [[Aurra Sing]], [[Bossk]], and [[Boba Fett]].<ref>{{TCW|R2 Come Home}}</ref> Multiple Klatooinians worked for [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]], including [[Barada]] and [[Kithaba]] who both [[Death|died]] during the [[Rescue of Han Solo]] at the [[Great Pit of Carkoon]].<ref name="Return of the Jedi">{{Film|VI}}</ref>

In [[9 BBY]],<ref name="Survivor date">{{JediSurvivorDate}}</ref> Klatooinian [[twin]]s [[Koob]] and [[Lizz]] were part of the [[Stinger Mantis crew|''Stinger Mantis'' crew]], led by [[Jedi Knight]] [[Cal Kestis]], under the directive of anti-Imperial freedom fighter [[Saw Gerrera]]. The twins helped Kestis access [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] intelligence on the [[T-2 Ramsidian-class yacht|yacht]] of [[Senator|Imperial Senator]] [[Daho Sejan]], disguising themselves as [[Coruscant Security Force]]s to trick the senator. Although the mission in the [[Coruscant Underworld]] was successful, the rebel crew was ambushed by the [[Ninth Sister]] of the [[Inquisitorius]], who killed the senator. Koob and Lizz attempted to fight the [[Dowutin]] [[Inquisitor]], but were killed in the chaos.<ref name="Survivor">''[[Star Wars Jedi: Survivor]]''</ref>

After the [[Battle of Endor|fall]] of the Galactic Empire, in [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Mando date">{{MandoDate|4}}</ref> a [[Unidentified Klatooinian raider captain|Klatooinian raider]] led a [[Klatooinian raiders|tribe]] on the [[swamp]] planet [[Sorgan]]. The tribe repurposed an [[AT-ST Raider|AT-ST]] [[walker]] and attacked a remote [[Unidentified village (Sorgan)|village]] several times before being defeated by the combined effort of [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty]] [[Hunting|hunter]] [[Din Djarin]], former [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebel]] [[shock trooper]] [[Carasynthia Dune|Cara Dune]], and the villagers during a [[skirmish on Sorgan]].<ref name="Chapter 4">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 4: Sanctuary}}</ref>

[[File:Don-Klatoo.png|thumb|right|240px|The Klatoonian Don negotiating with Boba Fett]]
The [[Tatooine Klatooinian family|Klatooinian family]] operated in the [[city]] of [[Mos Espa]] on the [[desert]] planet [[Tatooine]]. After Jabba the [[Hutt]] died during the [[Rescue of Han Solo|sail barge disaster]]<ref name="Storm">{{BOBF|Chapter 4: The Gathering Storm}}</ref> in [[4 ABY]]<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref>, his [[majordomo]],<ref name="Bib Databank">{{Databank|bib-fortuna|Bib Fortuna}}</ref> [[Bib Fortuna]], claimed the Hutt's throne, prompting the Klatooinian<ref name="Storm" /> [[Unidentified Klatooinian boss|don]]<ref name="CH4 audio description">{{BOBF|Chapter 4: The Gathering Storm}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> to quickly split his family from Jabba's [[Jabba's criminal empire|criminal empire]].<ref name="Storm" /> The Klatooinians gained control of the [[Mos Espa spaceport|spaceport]] and [[upper sprawl]].<ref name="Streets">{{BOBF|Chapter 3: The Streets of Mos Espa}}</ref> In 9 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]],<ref name="9 ABY">{{BoBFDate}}</ref> the Klatooinian family, [[Strassi family]], and [[Aqualish crime family|Aqualish family]] joined an alliance with [[Daimyo]] [[Boba Fett]]'s [[Fett gotra|gotra]], agreeing to stay neutral in the [[War against the Pykes|upcoming war]] against the [[Pyke Syndicate]].<ref name="Storm" /> The Klatooinian family later betrayed the gotra and forced two [[Gamorrean]] guards off the edge of a cliff, killing them. The don was later [[assassin]]ated by<ref name="Honor">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref> [[Master Assassin]]<ref name="Stranger">{{BOBF|Chapter 1: Stranger in a Strange Land}}</ref> [[Fennec Shand]], and the rest of the family submitted to the Fett Gotra.<ref name="Honor" />

In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> the Klatooinian [[Bolza Grool]] sold [[gorg]]s on the ''[[Colossus]],''<ref name="Bolza Grool">{{Databank|bolza-grool|Bolza Grool}}</ref> a [[supertanker fuel depot]] on the [[ocean]] planet [[Castilon]].<ref name="Recruit">{{Resistance|The Recruit}}</ref>

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[Skelly]], a [[human]] character from [[A New Dawn (novel)|''A New Dawn'']], was originally conceived as a Klatooinian. Despite this, author [[John Jackson Miller]] felt that he had an appearance that was somewhat Klatooinian.<ref name="blog">{{Faraway|url=fiction/books/swanewdawn.html|text=''Star Wars: A New Dawn''}}</ref> Skelly had a Klatooinian prosthetic right hand.<ref name="A New Dawn">[[A New Dawn (novel)|''A New Dawn'']]</ref>

